Found in the toolkit checkout (ue-llm-toolkit 9f6a0f7):
- MCPToolRegistry.cpp registers classes, not names: RegisterTool(MakeShared<FMCPTool_X>()), 43 times (FMCPTool_MetaSound only under #if UE >= 5.7; skill ue-metasounds already says so). The name is the Info.Name = TEXT("...") in Tools/MCPTool_X.h, or in Tools/MCPTool_X.cpp for niagara, lighting, asset, material. The lint reads the classes from the registry and the name from the class files, and demands exactly one name per class.
- Bridge (Plugin/UELLMToolkit/Resources/mcp-bridge/index.js): name: "unreal_status" (:82, :104) and "unreal_get_ue_context" (:119) are literals; registry tools appear there only as the template unreal_${tool.name}. The lint takes the literal unreal_* names minus the prefix, so toolkit_tools stays bare names.
- Count: 43 registered + 2 bridge (get_ue_context, status). Every toolkit_tools entry of the 19 skills that carry one resolves; an independent grep agrees.

Decisions (mine, not the maintainer):
- Comments are stripped before matching (// and /* */; double-quoted, single-quoted and template literals pass through untouched; a C++14 digit separator is not a literal), so a commented-out registration does not count. A registration under #if counts.
- What the parse cannot place (no registration, a class without exactly one Info.Name, no bridge tool, missing file) is t.Fatalf, not a skip: an upstream syntax change must stop the lint, not thin it.
- Checkout: UE_LLM_TOOLKIT wins (a relative value is taken from the repo root); else ue-llm-toolkit next to the repo root, then next to the main checkout when the root is a linked worktree (followed through the worktree pointer file and its commondir, read from disk, nothing executed). From .claude/worktrees/<name> the sibling is found without the env var.
- Stand-in tests that run in CI without the checkout: the parse over an fstest.MapFS with traps (#if, name in the .cpp, commented-out registration and bridge tool, unregistered header, comment openers inside literals, digit separator), its seven error cases, and mainCheckout over temp dirs (clone, worktree, relative pointer, submodule, none).

